  "query_preview": "..The main story over the next few days will be a\nbuilding area of high pressure across the Desert Southwest. This\nnearly 600 dam high will bring another round of very hot, very dry\nconditions to Utah. Extreme Heat Warnings remain in effect for the\nWasatch Front and portions of southern Utah, with many other areas\nunder Heat Advisories as early as Friday. No changes with this\npackage for the heat headlines.  \n\nA weak dry cold front will cross into northern Utah Sunday\nmorning, quickly retreating north before a stronger, but drier\ncold front crosses northern and central Utah Monday. With the\nnorthern stream remaining active, additional weak, dry cold fronts\nwill cross northern Utah through at least Tuesday. This will keep\ntemperatures around 5 to 8 degrees cooler than the very hot \ntemperatures over the weekend across northern and central Utah. \nSouthern utah will see less moderation, only around 1 to 3 \ndegrees. \n\nThe next potential monsoon surge looks to impact southern Utah as\nearly as mid to late week, with ensemble members currently split\nin timing, with around 50% of members indicating a monsoon surge\nwould start as early as next Thursday. That's the next real shot\nfor precipitation for most of the region, however. This long, hot,\ndry period will likely exasperate fire weather conditions once\nagain.",
